      "writtenOn": "2026-10-23T07:31:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When package-lock.json changes upstream, some dependencies may be replaced or dropped. How will `openbmc-autobump` handle orphaned/stale .bb recipes in `meta-phosphor/recipes-phosphor/webui-vue-npm/`? It might be worth documenting whether autobump will purge unreferenced recipe files in that subfolder during a bump commit to prevent abandoned recipes from accumulating in meta-phosphor.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 88,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 88,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "c10420b2845377e02bce9b17bcb8ed36d6eff5d9",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d8064b4b_e55d143a",
        "filename": "docs/designs/oss-license-sbom.md",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 88,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002106
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-23T14:04:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A bump does delete .bb files for packages that left the lockfile.\nAfter a regeneration, any .bb in that directory whose first line is # Generated by openbmc-autobump and whose name is not in the new set is removed. A hand-written recipe in the same directory is left alone. git add -A stages those deletions with the SRCREV bump. This only runs when the lockfile, toolchain roots, build host, or generator changed.\n \nI added this to the autobump bullet in the doc.",
